# threshold.config — global suppress / rate_filter / threshold directives.
# Loaded via suricata.yaml `threshold-file: /etc/suricata/threshold.config`
# (we bind-mount this file there in docker-compose).
#
# Use this for things that can't live inside a single rule: suppressing an
# upstream ET/abuse.ch SID we can't edit, or rate-limiting an alert across
# every rule. Our own honeypot-*.rules carry their thresholds inline.
#
# Syntax: https://docs.suricata.io/en/latest/configuration/global-thresholds.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPPRESS — silence alerts that are noise in this deployment.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The honeypot host talks to itself over WireGuard (10.8.0.0/24) for log
# shipping / health checks. Suppress our interaction telemetry for that range
# so internal traffic never looks like an attacker. (Adjust to your WG subnet.)
suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 92050100, track by_src, ip 10.8.0.0/24
suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 92050001, track by_src, ip 10.8.0.0/24

# Cloudflare health checks / Traefik ACME hit the web surface constantly.
# Suppress the "no SNI" scanner rule for Cloudflare ranges to cut false alarms.
# (Add the current Cloudflare ranges you actually front with — sample below.)
suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 92040040, track by_src, ip 173.245.48.0/20
suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 92040040, track by_src, ip 103.21.244.0/22

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RATE_FILTER — throttle alert volume during sustained floods so one attacker
# hammering a service can't drown EveBox. After `count` alerts in `seconds`,
# switch to `new_action` for `timeout` seconds. On a honeypot we keep the
# action as "alert" (never drop — we want the interaction) but this is where
# you'd change it if you later put Suricata inline/IPS.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# S7comm / Modbus write floods: after 20 alerts in 30s from a source, hold
# further alerts for 120s (dedupe the storm, keep the first evidence).
rate_filter gen_id 1, sig_id 92010004, track by_src, count 20, seconds 30, new_action alert, timeout 120
rate_filter gen_id 1, sig_id 92020006, track by_src, count 20, seconds 30, new_action alert, timeout 120
rate_filter gen_id 1, sig_id 92020007, track by_src, count 20, seconds 30, new_action alert, timeout 120

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THRESHOLD — global example (per-rule thresholds already live in the rules).
# Cap the generic S7comm tripwire so a chatty scan is one alert/min per source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 92010001, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 60
